  "honest_finding": [
    "The no-DP row measures whether this particular proximity attacker has a membership signal. Seed-level 95% confidence intervals expose the uncertainty instead of treating member\u00d7non-member pairs as independent.",
    "The formal privacy evidence is the R\u00e9nyi accountant's (epsilon, delta) bound for one full-participation Gaussian round, a public clip bound, and conservative replace-one client adjacency. It does not cover code outside this mechanism or an unaccounted training lifecycle.",
    "MIA AUC is only an empirical diagnostic for one attacker. A value near 0.5 cannot prove privacy; it can only show that this attack failed to distinguish the sampled cohorts. Throughput reports the corresponding utility cost."
